  <h2>Frequently asked questions</h2>
  <dl class="faq">
    <dt>Does the one-stop exception (wanstoppu) change the limit?</dt>
    <dd>No. It only shifts the whole credit onto resident tax; the 20%-of-levy cap logic is identical.</dd>
    <dt>We are a dual-income couple. How should we split donations?</dt>
    <dd>Credits attach to the person who donates, so compute the limit per earner and donate under each name separately.</dd>
    <dt>When do I see the money back?</dt>
    <dd>The income-tax part refunds after filing; the resident-tax part reduces next year's monthly instalments from June.</dd>
  </dl>

